cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use multipgs, please cite the method your analysis actually used. The references below cover the implemented estimators and their direct interpretation; there is no multipgs paper."
title: "multipgs: combining many polygenic scores into one"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that combines many polygenic scores into one: score stacking
  in a training cohort, a summary-statistic route over score-space moments, and
  training-free combination of same-trait scores, plus the machinery to acquire
  input scores and fold a fitted combination back into a single deployable
  per-variant weight file. Built on ldpred3 for genotype I/O, allele
  harmonisation, and the LDpred model behind score construction.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vilhjálmsson"
    given-names: "Bjarni Jóhann"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/multipgs"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.4.dev4
date-released: "2026-09-09"
keywords:
  - polygenic score
  - multi-PGS
  - meta-PGS
  - score stacking
  - elastic net
  - selection index
  - GWAS
